  "worked_solution": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(1,2,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(1,2).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,2) & =4(1)^{2}(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$",
